  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "With the introduction of the new CMA, the contentModel-resource-attribute disappeared and it has been replaced by \"hasModel\". However, the ResourceAttributeFinderModule was never called to resolve such an attribute during policy evaluation because it didn't register for it. ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The attached patch fixes the problem. It is now possible to write XACML policies that look at the content model(s) of an object like this:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "...",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<ResourceMatch MatchId=\"urn:oasis:names:tc:xacml:1.0:function:string-equal\">",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<AttributeValue DataType=\"",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": "\">info:fedora/cmodel:Container</AttributeValue>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<ResourceAttributeDesignator AttributeId=\"info:fedora/fedora-system:def/model#hasModel\"",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "DataType=\"",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
